    <div class="wrap article">
      <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Color</p>
      <h1>HEX, RGB and HSL Color Codes Explained</h1>
      <p class="lead">Every color on a screen is a mix of red, green and blue light. HEX, RGB and HSL are three ways of writing the same color. They are interchangeable, so choose whichever one suits the job.</p>

      <h2>HEX</h2>
      <p>A HEX code such as <code>#5B5BD6</code> is six digits in base 16. The first pair sets red, the second green and the third blue, each from 00 (none) to FF (full, which is 255). Three-digit codes such as <code>#FFF</code> are shorthand for <code>#FFFFFF</code>. HEX is compact and common in design tools and stylesheets.</p>

      <h2>RGB</h2>
      <p>RGB writes the same three channels as decimal numbers from 0 to 255, for example <code>rgb(91, 91, 214)</code>. Adding a fourth value, as in <code>rgba(91, 91, 214, 0.5)</code>, sets transparency. RGB is the easiest format to read when you are adjusting a single channel.</p>

      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>

      <h2>HSL</h2>
      <p>HSL describes a color the way people often think about it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hue</strong> is the position on the colour wheel, from 0 to 360 degrees. Red is 0, green is 120 and blue is 240.</li>
        <li><strong>Saturation</strong> is how strong or grey the colour looks, from 0% to 100%.</li>
        <li><strong>Lightness</strong> is how bright it is, from 0% (black) to 100% (white).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>HSL is useful for building palettes. To make a darker shade of a brand colour, keep the hue and saturation and lower the lightness.</p>

      <h2>Which one should you use?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use <strong>HEX</strong> when you copy a colour from a design tool.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>RGB</strong> when you need transparency or are working with code that expects channel values.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>HSL</strong> when you want to create lighter, darker or muted variations of one colour.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Try it yourself</h2>
      <p>The <a href="../tools/color-converter.html">Color Converter</a> updates all three formats at once. Pick a colour with the picker or type any value, then copy the one you need.</p>

      <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
